# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The max-cut problem {#the-max-cut-problem}"
msgstr "Ang max-cut problem {#the-max-cut-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The max-cut problem is a combinatorial optimization problem that is defined on a graph $G = (V, E)$, where $V$ is the set of vertices and $E$ is the set of edges. The goal is to partition the vertices into two sets, $S$ and $V \\setminus S$, such that the number of edges between the two sets is maximized.\n"
"For the detailed description of the max-cut problem, please refer to the [Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm) tutorial.\n"
"The max-cut problem is also used as an example in the [Advanced techniques for QAOA](/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa) tutorial.\n"
"In those tutorials, the QAOA algorithm is used to solve the max-cut problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang max-cut problem ay isang combinatorial optimization problem na tinukoy sa isang graph $G = (V, E)$, kung saan ang $V$ ay ang set ng mga vertex at ang $E$ ay ang set ng mga edge. Ang layunin ay hatiin ang mga vertex tungo sa dalawang set, $S$ at $V \\setminus S$, sa paraang ang bilang ng mga edge sa pagitan ng dalawang set ay napapalaki.\n"
"Para sa detalyadong paglalarawan ng max-cut problem, pakitingin ang tutorial na [Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm).\n"
"Ang max-cut problem ay ginagamit din bilang halimbawa sa tutorial na [Advanced techniques for QAOA](/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa).\n"
"Sa mga tutorial na iyon, ang QAOA algorithm ay ginagamit upang lutasin ang max-cut problem.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Graph -> Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Graph -> Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let us first consider a random graph with 100 nodes.\n"
msgstr "Una nating isaalang-alang ang isang random graph na may 100 node.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/37edb718-2bab-49d7-ad66-5f2f67d2aeff-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/37edb718-2bab-49d7-ad66-5f2f67d2aeff-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We encode the graph with 100 nodes into two-body Pauli-matrix correlations "
"across nine qubits (see the explanation below). The graph is represented as "
"a correlation matrix, where each node is encoded by a Pauli string. The sign"
" of the expectation value of the Pauli string indicates the partition of the"
" node. For example, node 0 is encoded by a Pauli string, $\\prod_0 = I_{8} "
"\\otimes ... I_2 \\otimes X_1 \\otimes X_0$. The sign of the expectation "
"value of this Pauli string indicates the partition of node 0. We define a "
"*Pauli-correlation encoding* (PCE) relative to $\\prod$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"Ine-encode natin ang graph na may 100 node tungo sa two-body Pauli-matrix "
"correlation sa siyam na qubit (tingnan ang paliwanag sa ibaba). Ang graph ay"
" kinakatawan bilang correlation matrix, kung saan ang bawat node ay ine-"
"encode ng isang Pauli string. Ang sign ng expectation value ng Pauli string "
"ay nagsasaad ng partition ng node. Halimbawa, ang node 0 ay ine-encode ng "
"isang Pauli string, $\\prod_0 = I_{8} \\otimes ... I_2 \\otimes X_1 \\otimes"
" X_0$. Ang sign ng expectation value ng Pauli string na ito ay nagsasaad ng "
"partition ng node 0. Tinutukoy natin ang *Pauli-correlation encoding* (PCE) "
"na nauukol sa $\\prod$ bilang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$ x_i \\coloneqq \\textit{sgn}(\\langle\\prod_i \\rangle), $$\n"
msgstr "$$ x_i \\coloneqq \\textit{sgn}(\\langle\\prod_i \\rangle), $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $x_i$ is the partition of node $i$ and $\\langle \\prod_i \\rangle \\coloneqq  \\langle \\psi |\\prod_i| \\psi \\rangle $ is the expectation value of the Pauli string encoding node $i$ over a quantum state $|\\psi \\rangle$.\n"
"Now, let's encode the graph into a Hamiltonian using PCE.\n"
"We divide the nodes into three sets: $S_1$, $S_2$, and $S_3$.\n"
"Then, we encode the nodes in each set using the Pauli strings with $X$, $Y$, and $Z$, respectively.\n"
"We need to extract a relationship between the number of nodes and qubits that we will need to encode all the nodes. Using all possible permutations for the encoding yields to:\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $x_i$ ay ang partition ng node $i$ at ang $\\langle \\prod_i \\rangle \\coloneqq  \\langle \\psi |\\prod_i| \\psi \\rangle $ ay ang expectation value ng Pauli string na nag-eencode ng node $i$ sa isang quantum state na $|\\psi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ngayon, i-encode natin ang graph tungo sa isang Hamiltonian gamit ang PCE.\n"
"Hinahati natin ang mga node tungo sa tatlong set: $S_1$, $S_2$, at $S_3$.\n"
"Pagkatapos, ine-encode natin ang mga node sa bawat set gamit ang mga Pauli string na may $X$, $Y$, at $Z$, ayon sa pagkakabanggit.\n"
"Kailangan nating makuha ang relasyon sa pagitan ng bilang ng mga node at qubit na kailangan natin upang ma-encode ang lahat ng node. Ang paggamit ng lahat ng posibleng permutasyon para sa encoding ay nagbibigay ng:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"m=3\\binom{n}{k}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"m=3\\binom{n}{k}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In this example we consider $k=2$, hence,\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawang ito, isinasaalang-alang natin ang $k=2$, kaya,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"m  = \\frac{3}{2} n(n-1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"m  = \\frac{3}{2} n(n-1).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the number of qubits $n$ needed to express a certain number of "
"nodes $m$ read as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Samakatuwid, ang bilang ng qubit na $n$ na kailangan upang ipahayag ang "
"isang tiyak na bilang ng node na $m$ ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"n = \\left\\lceil \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{1 + \\tfrac{8}{3}m}}{2} \\right\\rceil.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"n = \\left\\lceil \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{1 + \\tfrac{8}{3}m}}{2} \\right\\rceil.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Note that the $\\lceil \\cdot \\rceil$ symbol represents the ceiling "
"function, which rounds any real number up to the next integer. This ensures "
"that the number of qubits is an integer.*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Tandaan na ang simbolong $\\lceil \\cdot \\rceil$ ay kumakatawan sa ceiling"
" function, na inaangat ang anumang real number pataas sa susunod na integer."
" Tinitiyak nito na ang bilang ng qubit ay isang integer.*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang Problema para sa Quantum Hardware Execution "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit {#quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Quantum circuit {#quantum-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the state $|\\psi \\rangle$ is parameterized with $\\mathbf{\\theta}$, and we optimize these parameters $\\mathbf{\\theta}$ using a variational approach.\n"
"This tutorial employs the `efficient_su2` ansatz for our variational algorithm due to its expressive capabilities and ease of implementation.\n"
"We also use the relaxed loss function, which will be introduced later in this tutorial.\n"
"As a result, we can address large-scale problems with fewer qubits and shallower circuit depths.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, ang state na $|\\psi \\rangle$ ay may parameter na $\\mathbf{\\theta}$, at ino-optimize natin ang mga parameter na $\\mathbf{\\theta}$ na ito gamit ang variational approach.\n"
"Ang tutorial na ito ay gumagamit ng `efficient_su2` ansatz para sa ating variational algorithm dahil sa expressive capability at kadaling i-implement nito.\n"
"Ginagamit din natin ang relaxed loss function, na ipapakita pa sa tutorial na ito.\n"
"Bilang resulta, makakayanan nating lutasin ang mga large-scale problem gamit ang mas kaunting qubit at mas mababaw na circuit depth.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/035f6b4a-4de0-452a-b60f-7260f9e3103a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/pauli-"
"correlation-encoding-for-qaoa/extracted-"
"outputs/035f6b4a-4de0-452a-b60f-7260f9e3103a-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Loss function {#loss-function}"
msgstr "Loss function {#loss-function}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the loss function $\\mathcal{L}$, we use a relaxation of the max-cut objective function as described in [\\[1\\]](#references), which is defined as $\\mathcal{V}(\\mathbf{x}) \\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j}(1-x_i x_j)$. Here, $W_{i, j}$ denotes the weight of the edge $(i, j)$, and $x_i$ represents the partition of node $i$.\n"
"The loss function  $\\mathcal{L}$ is given by:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa loss function na $\\mathcal{L}$, gumagamit tayo ng relaxation ng max-cut objective function gaya ng inilarawan sa [\\[1\\]](#references), na tinutukoy bilang $\\mathcal{V}(\\mathbf{x}) \\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j}(1-x_i x_j)$. Dito, ang $W_{i, j}$ ay nagsasaad ng weight ng edge na $(i, j)$, at ang $x_i$ ay kumakatawan sa partition ng node $i$.\n"
"Ang loss function na $\\mathcal{L}$ ay ibinibigay sa pamamagitan ng:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\mathcal{L}\\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j} \\text{tanh} (\\alpha"
" \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle) \\text{tanh} (\\alpha \\langle\\prod_j \\rangle)"
" + \\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})},$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\mathcal{L}\\coloneqq \\sum_{(i, j) \\in E} W_{i, j} \\text{tanh} (\\alpha"
" \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle) \\text{tanh} (\\alpha \\langle\\prod_j \\rangle)"
" + \\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})},$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the max-cut objective function is replaced by the smooth hyperbolic "
"tangents of the expectation values of the Pauli strings encoding the nodes. "
"The regularization term $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ and the rescaling "
"factor $\\alpha$, proportional to the number of qubits, are introduced to "
"improve the solver's performance.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang max-cut objective function ay pinalitan ng smooth hyperbolic "
"tangent ng mga expectation value ng mga Pauli string na nag-eencode sa mga "
"node. Ang regularization term na $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ at ang "
"rescaling factor na $\\alpha$, na proporsyonal sa bilang ng mga qubit, ay "
"ipinakilala upang mapabuti ang performance ng solver.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The regularization term is defined as:\n"
msgstr "Ang regularization term ay tinutukoy bilang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ is defined as $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})} "
"\\coloneqq \\beta \\nu \\lbrack \\frac{1}{m} \\sum_{i \\in V} \\text{tanh} "
"(\\alpha \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle)^2 \\rbrack ^2$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})}$ ay tinutukoy bilang "
"$\\mathcal{L}^{(\\text{reg})} \\coloneqq \\beta \\nu \\lbrack \\frac{1}{m} "
"\\sum_{i \\in V} \\text{tanh} (\\alpha \\langle\\prod_i \\rangle)^2 \\rbrack"
" ^2$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\beta=1/2$, $\\nu = |E|/2 + (m -1) /4$, $|E|$ is the number of "
"edges, and $m$ is the number of nodes in the graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $\\beta=1/2$, $\\nu = |E|/2 + (m -1) /4$, ang $|E|$ ay ang "
"bilang ng mga edge, at ang $m$ ay ang bilang ng mga node sa graph.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 3: Magsagawa gamit ang Mga Qiskit Primitive {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we set `max_iter=50` in the optimization loop for "
"demonstration purposes. If we increase the number of iterations, we can "
"expect better results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa tutorial na ito, itinakda nating `max_iter=50` sa optimization loop para "
"sa demonstration purposes. Kung patatasin natin ang bilang ng mga iteration,"
" maaari tayong umasa ng mas magandang resulta.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 4: Mag-post-process at Ibalik ang Resulta sa Nais na Classical "
"Format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partitions of the nodes are determined by evaluating the sign of the "
"expectation values of the Pauli strings that encode the nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga partition ng mga node ay tinutukoy sa pamamagitan ng pagsusuri sa "
"sign ng mga expectation value ng mga Pauli string na nag-eencode sa mga "
"node.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can calculate the cut size of the max-cut problem using the partitions of"
" the node.\n"
msgstr ""
"Makakalkula natin ang cut size ng max-cut problem gamit ang mga partition ng"
" node.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once the training is complete, we perform one round of single-bit swap search to improve the solution as a classical post-processing step.\n"
"In this process, we swap the partitions of two nodes and evaluate the cut size. If the cut size is improved, we keep the swap. We repeat this process for all possible pairs of nodes connected by an edge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos matapos ang training, nagsasagawa tayo ng isang round ng single-bit swap search upang mapabuti ang solusyon bilang isang classical post-processing step.\n"
"Sa prosesong ito, pinag-papalitan natin ang mga partition ng dalawang node at sinusuri ang cut size. Kung ang cut size ay napabuti, pinapanatili natin ang swap. Inuulit natin ang prosesong ito para sa lahat ng posibleng pares ng mga node na konektado ng isang edge.\n"

